	<h2>Frequently Asked Questions About CRO</h2>

	<h3>What's the difference between CRO and traditional digital marketing?</h3>

	<p>
		Traditional digital marketing focuses on driving more traffic to your website through SEO, PPC, social media, and content marketing. CRO focuses on converting the traffic you already have into customers. Both are important, but CRO typically offers better ROI because it improves the performance of all your existing marketing channels.
	</p>

	<h3>How long does it take to see results from CRO?</h3>

	<p>
		Quick wins can happen within weeks (fixing obvious friction points, improving page speed, adding trust signals). However, meaningful, sustainable conversion rate improvements typically take 3-6 months of systematic testing and optimisation. The timeline depends on your traffic volume, test velocity, and baseline conversion rate.
	</p>

	<h3>What conversion rate should I expect for my e-commerce store?</h3>

	<p>
		E-commerce conversion rates vary widely by industry, average order value, and traffic source. Generally, 2-3% is average for e-commerce, 3-5% is good, and 5%+ is excellent. However, context matters - high-ticket items naturally convert lower than impulse purchases. Focus on improving YOUR conversion rate, not hitting an arbitrary benchmark.
	</p>

	<h3>Do you work with Shopify stores?</h3>

